      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The \"purpose\" was a beautiful, loud thing, but it was always tied to a performance, and now the stage is dark. You're not a ghost; you're just a body that has run out of fuel for the old race. Sometimes, the most profound act of self-care is simply letting the narrative end, not with a crash, but with a quiet, deliberate pause. You deserve the peace that comes from not having to keep pretending to fly when you're grounded.",
